  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Next\n\nFirst release. The engine behind the test adapters and the `coderules` CLI.\n\n- `AddCodeRuleEngine(solution, options)`: register rules with `AddRule`, `AddRules`, `AddRulePack` and `AddRulesFrom`; the solution is parsed once per run, contexts are shared and rules run in parallel.\n- Skips with a reason for a rule, pack, group or tag, optionally limited to a scope (`InProject`, `InNamespace`, `InPath`); `ExcludeFromAnalysis` takes files out of the analysis (experiments, generated code).\n- Accept single findings in the code with `[SuppressMessage]` or `#pragma warning disable`, always with a reason; rules can forbid it with `AllowSuppression => false`.\n- `ICodeRuleSetup`: one composition root per code rule project, read by the source generators, the test adapters and the CLI alike.\n- `ICodeRuleEngine` for own hosts: `RunAllAsync`, `RunAsync` with `RuleFilter`, the rule catalog and `EnsureSuccess`.\n- Human output and one JSON schema for AI agents (with a `rerun` command per result), switched with `UseOutputMode` or `CodeRuleSettings__OutputMode`.\n- `RuleTester<TRule>` for unit tests of single rules against inline code, independent of the test framework.",
